From: jason chien <3936511+jason5545@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:36:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] ARM64EC: drop the pending RF when the exception handler
 resumes somewhere other than the breakpoint

A breakpoint hit records HWBreakpointResumeRIP because RF does not survive Wine's ARM64EC context conversion, and the
breakpoint check consumes it only when execution reaches an armed address again. When the handler resumes elsewhere
(MSFS 2024's four-slot breakpoint handler emulates the function and returns to its caller), the record stayed and the
next call of the same function skipped its breakpoint, so the function body ran natively and the game read NULL
right after.

Reconcile in SyncThreadContext, which every NtContinue back into x64 code goes through: keep the pending RF only if
execution resumes at the breakpoint address, matching x86 where RF covers only the first instruction after the
handler returns. ehtest dr_skip: 500/1000 hits before, 1000/1000 after; dr_exec still 20001/20001.
---
 Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
index 6dd67b5d2..5be919849 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -1218,6 +1218,16 @@ extern "C" void SyncThreadContext(CONTEXT* Context) {
   uint32_t StateEFlags = CTX->ReconstructCompactedEFLAGS(Thread, false, nullptr, 0);
   Context->EFlags = (Context->EFlags & ECValidEFlagsMask) | (StateEFlags & ~ECValidEFlagsMask);
   Exception::LoadStateFromECContext(Thread, *Context);
+
+  // x86 debug register emulation (steamac-dr): a breakpoint hit leaves a pending RF for the breakpoint address
+  // (HWBreakpointResumeRIP), because RF itself does not survive Wine's ARM64EC context conversion. On x86, RF only
+  // covers the first instruction after the exception handler returns. When the handler resumes somewhere else, for
+  // example by emulating the whole function and returning to its caller as MSFS 2024's four-slot breakpoint handler
+  // does, the pending RF must go; otherwise the next call of the same function silently skips its breakpoint.
+  auto& ResumeRIP = Thread->CurrentFrame->State.HWBreakpointResumeRIP;
+  if (ResumeRIP != ~0ULL && ResumeRIP != Context->Rip) {
+    ResumeRIP = ~0ULL;
+  }
 }
 
 NTSTATUS ProcessInit() {
